{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The beast</b> — that which is not in settled areas, and every animal that is in settled areas, as in: \"and your animal and the beast that is in your land.\" Then he mentioned creeping things of the earth, and above it the bird, which is this: \"and winged bird.\" Then he mentioned all mankind, and began with the honored ones, who are kings of the earth and all nations under their hand, and then he mentioned princes — they are those who lord it over by force without justice, and corresponding to them, \"and all judges of the earth.\" And mankind, they are males and females; therefore —"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 148, :notes {0 "The comment ends with a dangling 'therefore —' (ולכן followed by a dash in the source); the text appears truncated."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:09.940565094Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}